<urn:atm:triage:finding/AW-INTEG-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AW-INTEG-002" ;
  triage:title "AW.5 test_cli_parity.py runs on one Python version in CI, not the 3.11-3.14 matrix the sprint doc promises" ;
  triage:description "phase-aw integration review (req-qa, at integrate/phase-aw 7845164e5): docs/plans/phase-aw/sprint-AW.5-native-tool-parity.md:61-62 states 'The test lives in crates/atm-graft-python/tests/test_cli_parity.py and is in the 3.11-3.14 matrix.' Independently confirmed false in .github/workflows/ci.yml: test_cli_parity.py is only run by the 'test' job (ci.yml:358, python -m unittest discover -s crates/atm-graft-python/tests -p test_cli_parity.py) which installs a single fixed interpreter (python-version: '3.14.7', ci.yml:220). The only job that actually matrices Python 3.11-3.14 is hermes-atm-abi3-compat (ci.yml:517-518), and that job's test step (ci.yml:539) discovers tests only from crates/hermes-atm/tests, never crates/atm-graft-python/tests -- it never runs test_cli_parity.py at all. So the CLI-parity test proving AC1/AC6 runs on exactly one Python version in CI, not the 3.11-3.14 range the sprint doc claims verifies it. Not a duplicate of ATM-QA-AW5R1-002 (closed), which only addressed 'the parity test never runs in CI at all' -- that closure's evidence does not mention a version-matrix requirement. Fix: either add test_cli_parity.py to the hermes-atm-abi3-compat job's matrix run (or an equivalent matrixed job), or correct the sprint doc's deliverable-3 text to state the actual single-version CI scope, with a QA pass on whichever correction is chosen." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-aw" ;
  triage:triageMode "integration_review" ;
  triage:category "ci" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-05T08:25:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AW-INTEGRATION-REVIEW ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-05T08:20:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AW-INTEG-002/INTEG-1> .

